  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="2d22e20e-0ccb-5169-8c51-a669f6007fd2" activityNameId="42497414-a625-5425-8091-342cf280e6ec" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Rape seed, at farm</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Rape seed, at farm
Inventory refers to the production of 1 kg rape seed, at farm with a moisture content of 6 %. Fresh matter yield at 12% moisture: 1258 kg/ha.;
UUID: 8b3db3b1-247a-327a-90c1-7136bc75da77
The inventory includes the processes of soil cultivation, sowing, weed control, fertilisation, pest and pathogen control and harvest. Machine infrastructure and a shed for machine sheltering is included. Inputs of fertilisers, pesticides and seed as well as their transports to the farm are considered. The direct emissions on the field are also included. The system boundary is at the farm gate.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Conventional production typical for the country. Water for irrigation is pumped from 48 meter depth by electric pumps.
Time period: The yield data have been collected for the years 2001-2006.
Production volume: US average prod of rape seed 1773t in 2001-2006. 
Sampling: Data come from the NREL database and from varoius U.S database. Data were compiled from statistics, literature, farm survey reports, documents from extension services, and expert knowledge. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8b3db3b1-247a-327a-90c1-7136bc75da77.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
